  "title": "Exact Counting Formulas for Two-Black-Square Crossword Rook Placements",
  "batch_label": "50",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every integer n>=3 and every unordered pair B of black squares in an n by n grid, |RP(G_B)| is given by the exhaustive coordinate-dependent factorial formulas (C), (E), (S), and (I) in evidence/factorial_formulas.md, together with the opposite-corner and exceptional common-boundary-row/column formulas proved in evidence/finite_census.md; every remaining relative-position class has value zero because its across- and down-word counts differ. Formula (I) distinguishes the parallel and crossed orders of two nonattacking interior squares. This claim is a complete exact counting formula for every two-black-square configuration, but it does not assert or prove the all-n discrete maximum M_2(n) or its equality classification.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
